{"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNotations\/Item\/arpeggiate(_:)"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"arpeggiate","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLArpeggiate","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLArpeggiateV"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"case","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"title":"MXLNotations.Item.arpeggiate(_:)","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLNotationsV4ItemO10arpeggiateyAeA13MXLArpeggiateVcAEmF","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"arpeggiate","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLArpeggiate","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLArpeggiateV"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"roleHeading":"Case"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnotations\/item\/arpeggiate(_:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNotations","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNotations\/Item"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"arpeggiate"},{"text":" alternative.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLArpeggiate":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlarpeggiate","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The arpeggiate type indicates that this note is part of an arpeggiated chord. The number attribute can be used"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to distinguish between two simultaneous chords arpeggiated separately (different numbers) or together (same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"number). The direction attribute is used if there is an arrow on the arpeggio sign. By default, arpeggios go"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the lowest to highest note. The length of the sign can be determined from the position attributes for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"arpeggiate elements used with the top and bottom notes of the arpeggiated chord. If the unbroken attribute is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"set to yes, it indicates that the arpeggio continues onto another staff within the part. This serves as a hint"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to applications and is not required for cross-staff arpeggios."}],"title":"MXLArpeggiate","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLArpeggiate","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLArpeggiate","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNotations":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNotations"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNotations"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Notations refer to musical notations, not XML notations. Multiple notations are allowed in order to represent","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"multiple editorial levels. The print-object attribute, added in Version 3.0, allows notations to represent","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"details of performance technique, such as fingerings, without having them appear in the score.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnotations","title":"MXLNotations","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNotations","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNotations/Item":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Item"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Item"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnotations\/item","abstract":[{"text":"One of the alternatives for Notations.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLNotations.Item","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNotations\/Item","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","title":"IvorMXL","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNotations/Item/arpeggiate(_:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"arpeggiate"},{"type":"text","text":" alternative."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNotations\/Item\/arpeggiate(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnotations\/item\/arpeggiate(_:)","title":"MXLNotations.Item.arpeggiate(_:)","role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"arpeggiate","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLArpeggiateV","text":"MXLArpeggiate","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}]}}}